# Site and publish

## Source of truth

Edit `pa_edu/web/` (`app.js`, `app.css`, `index.html`). `pde_site/` is generated and gitignored. `python -m pa_edu.publish` copies web assets, writes `data/index.json.gz` + `data/lea/<aun>.json.gz` from parquet, and writes the download portal. It does not copy the tree to elm. nginx `gzip_static` in the image serves the `.json` URLs. Leave Parquet uncompressed on disk.

## Download portal

`pde_site/download/` is a separate page from the LEA browser: Parquet tables, one zip per directory county, `schema.sql`, and `pdenumbers.duckdb`. Edit copy and packing in `pa_edu/portal.py`, view SQL in `sql/portal.sql`, and portal CSS in `pa_edu/web/download.css`. Bump `ASSET_VERSION` in `portal.py` when `download.css` changes.

Keep the portal in the same change as a new or reshaped table:

- One sentence in `TABLES`. The keys must match `refine.COLUMNS`. An unknown parquet file fails the build.
- `aun` tables are filtered to `lea.county` (the administrative office). Millage rows stay with that county. Tables with no `aun` are lookups: add them to `LOOKUP_TABLES` or the county build fails.
- New views go in `sql/portal.sql` with `-- view:`, `-- needs:`, and `-- about:`. They keep published grain. Do not sum budget with actuals, or a parent account with its children.
- SPA links to `download/` use class `site-link`.

The DuckDB views read `https://pdenumbers.org/download/tables/*.parquet`. DuckDB opens each file while the view is created. `python -m pa_edu.portal` is a local preview and points that database at local files. Do not put the preview database in the image.

## JSON shape

- Publish reads parquet (via DuckDB), not the locked `pde.duckdb` file contents beyond what refine wrote.
- Attach Act 1, millage, and similar sidecars only onto years that already exist (budget / actual / enrollment). Do not create sidecar-only years.
- Keep precise rates in JSON (mills to 4 decimals). Do not run millage through helpers that round money to 2 decimals.
- Catalog `sources` in `index.json` should link the workbook URL for the series (per-year when files are yearly).

## UI habits

- Budget card notes: year-over-year change, then Act 1, then mills. Multi-rate districts list each county/place line.
- Keep the `site-foot` source-code footnote in `index.html` (outside `#app`) so every SPA view links to the GitHub repo.
- Bump `app.js?v=` / `app.css?v=` in `index.html` whenever those files change so elm visitors are not stuck on a cached script.
- After deploy, prove with http://192.168.10.116:8090/.

## Deploy note

A push to `main` is the deploy. The education agent runs `refine`, `personnel`, and `check` against `/home/jenkins/pde-data`, then `python -m pa_edu.publish`. That writes `pde_site/` and does not rsync it to elm. The job pushes `192.168.150.59:443/pdenumbers:<git sha>` and runs `scripts/docker09.sh`, which starts `pdenumbers` on port 8090 if it is absent and replaces that container if it is already running. Do not run publish from an agent session, and do not copy `data/` from the laptop.

`refine` and `personnel` download a source file only when the education cache does not already have it. To build without deploying, call `main` with `deploy` monkeypatched, or run `python -m pa_edu.portal` for the download directory only.
